  "Question": "Express \\(1/(x^2-x)\\) and \\(1/(x^2-1)\\) with a common denominator. Let their least common denominator be the polynomial \\(P\\). What is the value of \\(P\\) when \\(x=3\\)?",
  "Choices": {},
  "Correct Answer": "24",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "Since \\(x^2-x=x(x-1)\\) and \\(x^2-1=(x-1)(x+1)\\), the least common denominator is \\(P=x(x-1)(x+1)\\). When \\(x=3\\), \\(P=3\\times2\\times4=24\\).",
